WEBVTT

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:21.270
<i>Oh, there's some.</i>

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:35.740
<i>Great, this is a big haul.</i>

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:39.200
<i>Okay, I'll drop these off,
then search for some sauna stones.</i>

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:23.760
AUTUMNAL EQUINOX

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:34.610
Gosh, that was a surprise.

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:36.990
Thanks for saving me.

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.610
I noticed you were taking too long
to come back up.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.030
Arashi.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.370
You keep a knife on you,
so why didn't you use it?

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:47.410
You're right. I do.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:49.250
I totally forgot.

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:50.500
You forgot?

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:54.210
I've never had the need to use
a knife regularly until we came here.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.380
So I haven't gotten used to it yet.

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:59.670
<i>Hana seemed well accustomed
to using it, though.</i>

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:03.680
<i>You really can't even manage
a minor hazard like this?</i>

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:05.930
<i>Is that the best you can do, Arashi?</i>

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:08.430
But I managed to gather
a lot of shellfish.

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:11.690
<i>I wonder how he would react
if I just told him everything.</i>

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.810
<i>"Your precious Hana is dead.</i>

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:17.070
<i>And we're the ones who killed her."</i>

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:21.490
Does your hand hurt?

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:22.780
What?

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:25.160
Sometimes you look like
you're in a lot of pain.

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:26.200
Not really.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:29.660
If I go about things normally,
I don't feel any pain at all.

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:31.080
Well, that's good to hear.

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:34.630
Okay, I'm going back down
to gather some stones for the sauna.

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:36.960
Don't you think you should call it quits?

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:38.590
Haven't you realized it's dangerous?

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:41.930
Sorry, it's just too fun for me to quit.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:43.840
I'll be more careful this time.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:46.930
<i>Fun?</i>

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:48.600
<i>What the hell does that mean?</i>

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:50.640
<i>You almost drowned.
Are you just that stupid?</i>

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:52.690
<i>On top of that, the others...</i>

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:56.520
<i>They didn't even notice
that Arashi almost drowned.</i>

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:58.190
<i>What is their deal?</i>

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:01.400
<i>How have they even survived
this long out here?</i>

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:02.900
Awesome!

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:05.700
We have to heat these stones up
in the stove first, right?

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:08.620
Be careful. Some stones break apart
when they get heated.

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:10.080
Understood!

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:12.120
I'll make sure
there's proper ventilation too, sir.

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:13.790
"Sir"?

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.130
<i>Letting them get close does us no good.</i>

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.300
Can you really manage to be careful,
Semimaru?

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:25.640
Man, I never thought we would have
the chance to enjoy a sauna.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:28.100
I have never been in a sauna before.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:29.390
Seriously?

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:31.140
Then you've got a lot to look forward to.

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:33.520
And of course, ladies go first.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.650
Even though I'm doing all the work.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:36.650
Well, whatever.

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:47.120
Hey, Nat, let's hit the sauna.

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:48.660
It's my...

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:50.540
Oh, shoot.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.250
There will be other chances
to use the sauna, I'm sure.

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:57.790
Bring a chair so we have a spot
to leave our clothes outside.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:59.540
Has anyone seen the deck of cards?

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:00.670
Not me.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:02.010
The stones are ready.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:03.760
They're burning hot.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.050
Okay, pour in the water.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.970
But only use a little,
so we don't waste any.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:15.480
Your work is done. See you later, Semmy.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:17.350
It's the girls' time now.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:18.600
Don't push!

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:23.900
This feels amazing!

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:28.530
Why does it come
at the worst possible times?

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:31.410
I really wanted to try out the sauna.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:38.290
<i>My body still reacts once a month,
even though I've lost any sense of time.</i>

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:40.880
<i>How annoying.</i>

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:42.800
<i>Especially since we're on a ship.</i>

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:45.840
<i>I can't afford to get anything dirty
since laundry isn't easy to do.</i>

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:48.090
It's so hot!

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:50.180
-I can't take it anymore!
-Let's go jump in the sea!

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:58.940
<i>I read somewhere that
it can be dangerous during your period</i>

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:00.980
<i>since the smell of blood
attracts wild animals.</i>

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:04.230
<i>Is that true out here too?</i>

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:09.990
<i>At one point in history, women were locked
in small huts during their periods.</i>

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:12.450
<i>I read that somewhere.</i>

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:17.710
<i>Speaking of books,
I haven't read any recently.</i>

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:20.670
<i>There were how-to books
in the storage room we found,</i>

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:22.630
<i>but no novels.</i>

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:24.750
<i>No picture books...</i>

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:27.130
<i>or even mysteries.</i>

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:30.510
<i>I'll never have the chance
to read those again.</i>

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:34.430
Sweet! It's finally our turn!

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:36.310
Would you care to join us, sirs?

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:41.310
You go in first.

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:43.230
Right.

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:44.820
Oh, this is awesome!

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:46.610
It's an honest to goodness sauna.

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:50.070
And it's all thanks to my skills
in heating the stones.

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:52.780
Don't forget I'm the one
who got the stones in the first place.

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:55.160
Then this is thanks
to the both of us, together.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:02.250
Impressive. That's a chiseled body
you've got there, sir.

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:07.880
It's so hot.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:10.760
It's hot! But you know, it works wonders.

00:07:14.510 --> 00:07:16.810
What? You're done already, sir?

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:20.980
Time to switch.

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:22.650
Sure.

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:30.110
Can't compete with that.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:33.490
Hey, why didn't the two of you
just come in together?

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:40.500
A sauna can suddenly affect your health,
and accidents are common.

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:44.380
We alternate so that the other can react
if something bad happens.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:46.340
I get it!

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:49.420
Speaking of which,

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:51.550
I notice you always keep
a close eye on Ango.

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:54.890
I know he's injured right now,

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:56.760
but is something else worrying you?

00:07:57.970 --> 00:08:00.310
Ango never really watches you, though.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:04.150
For some reason,
he's only focused on Natsu.

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:07.650
What for? Your friend has bad taste!

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:09.780
Ango...

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:14.110
left some unfinished business behind
in the old world.

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:17.620
Then he must be happy.

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:22.620
You know, humans are the happiest
when they regret something.

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:26.710
Oh, I think I know what you mean by that.

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:30.630
I'm not so sure you do, Arashi.
You're way too optimistic.

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:33.130
I get it... probably.

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:38.350
Oh, I've had enough too. I'm getting out.

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:40.640
Jeez, how pathetic can you get?

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:42.140
What about you?

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:44.270
I'm going to tough it out a bit more.

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:45.980
I'll show you all what a real man is like.

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:48.730
This isn't an endurance competition,
you know.

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:52.900
Then let's make it one next time.
Hurry up and shut the door.

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:54.030
Sure thing.

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:58.990
Damn, it's hot. Super hot.

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:01.240
But I'm not done yet.

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:03.120
I'm burning up!
I've got to get in the sea!

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:05.710
Okay, let's go.

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:11.880
I said something I shouldn't have.

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:23.560
What are you doing out here?

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:25.060
Drawing a picture.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:27.400
Aren't you going to go in?

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:29.110
The sauna?

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:33.650
No, I avoid getting naked in the presence
of others as much as possible.

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:38.910
I took a bath earlier and, right now,
I'd like to focus on drawing.

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:41.870
Don't you think you're just
wasting time with that?

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:44.370
Surely there must be other things
you should be doing.

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:47.250
Time is a strange thing.

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:51.000
There are times where hours and hours
pass without me even realizing it.

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:53.670
Other times I feel like I've drawn a lot,

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:56.510
but I'm surprised
at how little time has passed.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:00.720
That's why I've been thinking...

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:04.220
If I spent a whole hour
in a state of pure focus,

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:07.520
worked to enrich just a minute
of that entire hour,

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:12.230
and used one second of that minute
with a profound level of care...

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:15.990
then maybe time itself
would cease to pass at all.

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:19.700
Perhaps we just think
that time has a limit,

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:22.330
but in fact, it's actually limitless.

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:24.990
I don't understand what you mean.

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:27.710
Well, I don't really get it either.

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:34.960
<i>Chimaki, if you had been
in the facility with us,</i>

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:37.630
<i>I have no doubt
you would have failed in an instant.</i>

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:45.220
I guess that's enough for Mr. Semimaru.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:48.390
I bet that was a good detox for my system.

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:53.020
Weird. It won't open.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:55.480
Arashi! Enough with the pranks!

00:10:56.070 --> 00:10:57.360
Who's out there holding it shut?

00:10:57.570 --> 00:10:58.990
Open up already!

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:02.070
Wait, Arashi isn't the type of guy
to do something like this.

00:11:02.570 --> 00:11:04.830
Matsuri? It couldn't be Chimaki.

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:06.950
Or Big Sis or Natsu.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:11.330
The only one
who does shit like this is me.

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:12.920
Does that mean the door is busted?

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:16.420
Oh, crap! Somebody get me out of here!

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:17.800
Oh, right.

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:19.590
There's a door on the ceiling, too.

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:23.550
Seriously? This one won't open either?

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:25.050
Why?

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:29.600
Damn it! What the hell?

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:35.860
Somebody save me!

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:40.280
I don't see Natsu. Where is she?

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:43.860
Nat isn't feeling very well,
so she's resting in her room right now.

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:51.120
I dozed off.

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:55.210
<i>In the past, I used to struggle
with the feeling of loneliness</i>

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:58.050
<i>after being left out like this.</i>

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:03.380
<i>But right now, I'm really
not that worried about any of that.</i>

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:05.640
What?

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:09.970
Be more attentive.

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:15.400
What's wrong? Are you okay?

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:17.480
I heard you weren't feeling well.

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:19.230
Oh, I'm fine.

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:24.610
Oh, did you hear a sound?
Like someone knocking on a door just now?

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:25.820
No.

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:28.450
I see. Maybe I imagined it.

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:31.040
I'm going to go check.

00:12:33.460 --> 00:12:34.580
The sauna room?

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:45.840
Semimaru!

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:49.680
<i>Hurry and get some water!</i>

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:52.680
Seawater is fine!
Just hurry and pour it on him!

00:12:53.270 --> 00:12:54.480
We have to cool him off! Hurry!

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:56.730
How about tossing him in the bathtub?

00:12:57.190 --> 00:12:58.110
Good idea.

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:02.110
Bring him drinking water too!

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:03.690
He needs to rehydrate!

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:13.500
Oh, thank god.

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:17.580
Hey, Ryo.

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:23.840
It's just like you said,
a sauna is a dangerous place.

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:26.970
From now on, no one goes in alone.

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:29.180
And no endurance competitions either.

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:31.100
Okay.

00:13:32.180 --> 00:13:34.350
Natsu, you look pale as a ghost.

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:38.020
Please just drink some more water.

00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:40.610
I'm already filled to the brim.

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:43.190
Just drink.

00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:47.200
This isn't anything to cry over.

00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:50.490
Dummy.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:55.000
Hey, Nat.

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:56.330
Let them be alone for a bit.

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:57.710
What?

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:00.210
What's that mean?

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:02.880
What?

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:04.300
What?

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:12.430
Excuse me, Ryo? Will we be
keeping the ship here for the time being?

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:15.310
I'd say so.
At least until Semimaru has recovered.

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:17.980
All right, then I'll dive
and look for something useful.

00:14:18.270 --> 00:14:20.600
Sure. Be careful out there.

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:27.700
Can't forget to bring the knife.

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:42.330
The misfortune I sensed before we set sail

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:45.300
must be all of these accidents
that keep happening.

00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:49.760
But that has nothing to do
with Ango and Ryo, right?

00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:51.720
They helped save us, after all.

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:54.560
Yes, right.

00:14:56.180 --> 00:14:58.930
Hey, talk about something. I'm bored.

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:04.770
Well, is it true that you used to be
bullied a lot when you were younger?

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:06.690
That's what you want to talk about?

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:10.240
Well, I had no father at home,

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:13.490
and Mom was a club hostess
who jumped from one boyfriend to the next.

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:18.700
Normal parents wouldn't want their kids
to be friends with someone like me.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:22.630
Stupid parents put thoughts
into their heads,

00:15:22.710 --> 00:15:25.040
so their stupid kids bullied me.

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:29.880
Back in elementary, I just dealt with it.

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:32.340
But in middle school,
I started to turn delinquent.

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:34.760
Then I figured it all out.

00:15:34.890 --> 00:15:35.970
What?

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:39.600
I realized a world
outside of school exists,

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:41.560
so I ignored the jerks.

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:47.440
Well, even worse bullies exist
in the outside world.

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:49.900
But there are some people
who aren't total idiots.

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:54.660
<i>Sometimes you even meet people
like Arashi out here.</i>

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:59.830
If you know what it's like to be bullied,
then why do you bully others?

00:16:01.370 --> 00:16:03.120
I haven't bullied you at all lately.

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:04.750
You just did.

00:16:05.830 --> 00:16:07.750
There are two types of people.

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:11.340
Those who were bullied and refuse
to put others through the same experience,

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:15.590
<i>and those who were bullied and believe it
gives them the right to do it to others.</i>

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:22.020
Regardless, neither of them realize
that they've let themselves be trapped.

00:16:23.890 --> 00:16:26.270
I just said something really deep.

00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:33.360
The wind has started to pick up.
Let's raise the sails and start moving.

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:50.750
How is Semimaru doing?

00:16:51.340 --> 00:16:52.380
Oh, hi, Ango.

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:55.300
Semimaru said that he feels fine,

00:16:56.390 --> 00:16:59.140
though he got tired and fell asleep.
I hope he's okay.

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:02.850
He drank plenty of water,
so I don't think we need to worry.

00:17:03.730 --> 00:17:05.100
Let him rest for now.

00:17:05.890 --> 00:17:10.860
Oh, I wanted to thank you
for carrying Semimaru out here.

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:14.860
Don't mention it. I'm impressed
you noticed there was a problem, Natsu.

00:17:15.650 --> 00:17:19.370
It's because I remembered
what you said about being attentive.

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:21.370
You need to be alert.

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:25.080
Unless you notice the constant changes
in your surroundings,

00:17:25.330 --> 00:17:26.460
you could lose your life.

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:29.630
Oh, right. I'll do my best.

00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:33.630
Yes. I'll do my best, Ango.

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:37.430
Ango?

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:40.760
This team is really lacking.

00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:42.720
What kind of training did you get?

00:17:43.220 --> 00:17:45.140
I'm sorry.

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:47.140
We didn't train.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:50.860
Apparently, our team is composed
entirely of dropouts.

00:17:51.650 --> 00:17:52.820
"Dropouts"?

00:17:53.820 --> 00:17:57.990
Summer A is an elite team, right?
That's what Ms. Botan told us.

00:17:58.570 --> 00:18:04.540
Our Team B is full of people who didn't
really fit in well in the old world.

00:18:05.040 --> 00:18:09.120
Apparently, they felt the non-elite
should be part of the insurance plan too.

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:17.630
Do you really think dropouts
should've been allowed to come here?

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:22.140
I'm so sorry.
I totally agree that it was a bad idea.

00:18:22.720 --> 00:18:25.310
They should have sent people
who were more useful instead.

00:18:25.770 --> 00:18:28.020
The people who chose us
definitely made a mistake.

00:18:28.730 --> 00:18:29.900
So basically,

00:18:30.650 --> 00:18:34.820
not only are you civilians,
but you're all worthless as well.

00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:36.400
Is that right?

00:18:39.110 --> 00:18:41.030
Well, that's true for me.

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:44.030
But not for Arashi and the others...

00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:46.540
Wait...

00:18:48.910 --> 00:18:51.040
<i>It's true that I'm a dropout,</i>

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:54.040
<i>but I've been improving
ever since we came here.</i>

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:56.380
<i>Without a doubt.</i>

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:04.760
Ango?

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:07.310
If they were going to send dropouts...

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:11.310
<i>then why couldn't it have been them?</i>

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:15.900
No!

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:21.030
The worst part is that these dropouts
are still somehow able to survive!

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:25.240
<i>All the other teams were out there
living happy lives!</i>

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:26.740
<i>Even though they're amateurs!</i>

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:29.040
<i>They were even having kids!</i>

00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:33.880
So why the hell did we go through
all that training?

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:36.210
Was the test we suffered even necessary?

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:38.170
Was it all for nothing?

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:41.180
No...

00:19:42.510 --> 00:19:43.930
This is all too much...

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:50.520
I'm starving.

00:19:51.890 --> 00:19:54.440
So if Semmy is still recovering
from earlier, then...

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:57.320
does that mean Arashi is the one
who's cooking today?

00:19:57.520 --> 00:19:58.650
I think so.

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:01.200
Okay, then where is Arashi now?

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:03.360
Arashi!

00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:06.070
Arashi, where's lunch?

00:20:06.530 --> 00:20:08.040
Arashi!

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:11.500
Arashi is missing?

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:13.460
Yes, we can't find him.

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:15.380
He has to be somewhere.

00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:17.880
But we've already looked everywhere.

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:21.380
It took you too long to notice.

00:20:21.880 --> 00:20:24.050
We already looked
in all the storage rooms.

00:20:25.220 --> 00:20:27.510
When we heard that Semmy had collapsed,

00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:30.020
Arashi came back up with us
from the water, right?

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:32.140
And he was here after that, right?

00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:35.520
You don't think he went diving again?

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:37.900
Not without telling one of us.

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:41.240
But wait, that has to be the answer.

00:20:41.650 --> 00:20:44.700
If he's not here on the ship, then...

00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:47.660
he's in the sea.

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:54.120
No way!

00:20:54.210 --> 00:20:56.630
Stop standing there! Turn the ship around!

00:20:57.170 --> 00:20:58.290
Don't order me around.

00:20:58.380 --> 00:21:00.090
We have to go and find Arashi!

00:21:00.170 --> 00:21:03.760
You realize that, even if we go back,
we can't follow the exact same path.

00:21:04.090 --> 00:21:05.590
Whatever! Just turn us around!

00:21:12.180 --> 00:21:14.770
Everybody, keep your eyes open
and search the sea!

00:21:14.850 --> 00:21:16.190
We have to find Arashi!

00:21:17.480 --> 00:21:18.690
Arashi!

00:21:18.770 --> 00:21:20.270
Hey, Arashi!

00:21:20.360 --> 00:21:21.690
Arashi!

00:21:21.820 --> 00:21:23.240
Arashi...

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:28.490
Arashi!

00:21:46.260 --> 00:21:47.430
Where's the ship?

00:21:48.180 --> 00:21:49.260
Where did it go?

00:21:54.890 --> 00:21:58.900
If I remember right,
we left the east shore and sailed north.

00:21:59.100 --> 00:22:00.520
So if I swim west,

00:22:01.360 --> 00:22:03.780
I should reach the shore, hopefully.

00:22:03.860 --> 00:22:06.190
But which way is west?

00:22:07.990 --> 00:22:09.410
The sun sets in the west.

00:22:18.250 --> 00:22:19.370
What should I do?
